0..75 Comment "// A case on a vector checks each arm at the fields of its own constructor."
76..78 Comment "//"
79..156 Comment "// A case on an indexed family works as a case on a family with no indices. A"
157..225 Comment "// case may still write an arm whose constructor cannot stand at the"
226..304 Comment "// scrutinee\'s index, as `oneLength` does. `vector-head.gandr` leaves that arm"
305..312 Comment "// out."
313..315 Comment "//"
316..388 Comment "// An arm may return a constructor at a length that a call computes. The"
389..461 Comment "// `VCons` arm of `vappend` returns `VCons` at `plus(m, Succ(k))`, which"
462..505 Comment "// computes the length that `VCons` states."
506..508 Comment "//"
509..587 Comment "// - see: Dybjer, _Inductive families_, FAC 1994, doi:10.1007/BF01211308 — a"
588..650 Comment "//   case that checks each arm at its own constructor\'s fields"
651..728 Comment "// - see: #3627 — a constructor at a length written as a call that computes"
729..754 Comment "//   the length it states"
756..793 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
